DG.put("krisnaavtaar/55",{"n":55,"title":"ਅਥ ਦ੍ਵਾਦਸ ਭੂਪ ਜੁਧ ਕਥਨ","title_roman":"Ath dvaadas bhoop judh kathan","page":539,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1274],"number_text":"੧੨੭੪।","page":539,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦ੍ਵਾਦਸ ਭੂਪ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਦਸਾ ਤਿਹ ਦਾਤਨ ਪੀਸ ਕੈ ਕੋਪ ਕੀਯੋ।","roman":"Dvaadas bhoop nihaari dasaa tih daatan pees kai kop keeyo |","meaning_en":"Seeing their plight, the twelve kings ground their teeth in fury.","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰੀਆ ਸਬ ਹੀ ਬਰ ਅਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੇ ਬਹੁ ਸਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੈ ਦਲ ਬਾਟਿ ਦੀਯੋ।","roman":"Dhareeaa sab hee bar atran ke bahu sastran kai dal baati deeyo |","meaning_en":"All of them bore fine missiles, and they shared out many weapons among the army.","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਰੀਆ...ਅਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੇ: read as 'holders of fine missiles (astras)'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਲਿ ਆਪ ਬਿਖੈ ਤਿਨ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੀਯੋ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਅਤਿ ਛੋਭ ਸੋ ਤਾਤੋ ਹੀਯੋ।","roman":"Mili aap bikhai tin mantr keeyo kari kai ati chhobh so taato heeyo |","meaning_en":"They took counsel together, their hearts hot with great agitation:","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਰਿ ਹੈ ਮਰਿ ਹੈ ਭਵ ਕੋ ਤਰਿ ਹੈ ਜਸ ਸਾਥ ਭਲੋ ਏਕ ਜੀਯੋ। ੧੨੭੪।","roman":"Lari hai mari hai bhav ko tari hai jas saath bhalo ek jeeyo | 1274 |","meaning_en":"\"We will fight, we will die, we will cross the ocean of existence; it is good to live even once with glory.\"","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਸ ਸਾਥ ਭਲੋ ਏਕ ਜੀਯੋ: read as 'better to live (even briefly) with glory'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1275],"number_text":"੧੨੭੫।","page":539,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਧਰਿ ਆਇ ਅਰੇ ਸੁ ਘਨੋ ਦਲੁ ਲੈ ਹਰਿ ਪੇਖਿ ਹਕਾਰੋ।","roman":"Yau man mai dhari aai are su ghano dalu lai hari pekhi hakaaro |","meaning_en":"Resolving this in their minds, they came with a great army, stood firm, and seeing Krishna, challenged him:","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾਹੀ ਹਨੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਪਾਚ ਅਬੈ ਹਮ ਸੰਗ ਲਰੋ ਹਰਿ ਭ੍ਰਾਤਿ ਤੁਮਾਰੋ।","roman":"Yaahee hane nrip paach abai ham sang laro hari bhraati tumaaro |","meaning_en":"\"It is this brother of yours who slew the five kings; now let him fight us, Krishna,","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as referring to Balram; the line could also be taken as an address to Krishna himself."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਤਰ ਆਇ ਭਿਰੋ ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਨਹਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਛਾਡ ਕੈ ਧਾਮਿ ਸਿਧਾਰੋ।","roman":"Naatar aai bhiro tum hoon nahi aayudh chhaad kai dhaami sidhaaro |","meaning_en":"or else come and fight us yourself; if not, lay down your weapons and go home.","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਤੁਮ ਮੈ ਬਲੁ ਹੈ ਘਟਿਕਾ ਲਰਿ ਕੈ ਲਖਿ ਲੈ ਪੁਰਖਤ ਹਮਾਰੋ। ੧੨੭੫।","roman":"Jo tum mai balu hai ghatikaa lari kai lakhi lai purkhat hamaaro | 1275 |","meaning_en":"If you have strength, fight for a ghari and see our manliness.\"","page":539,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Ghari: a measure of time, about 24 minutes."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1276],"number_text":"੧੨੭੬।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਿਨ ਕੀ ਸਬ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਹਰਿ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Yau suni kai bateeyaa tin kee sab aayudh lai hari saamuhe aayo |","meaning_en":"Hearing their words, Krishna took up all his weapons and came before them.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਹਿਬ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੋ ਸੀਸ ਕਟਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਸਦਾ ਸਿੰਘ ਮਾਰ ਕੈ ਭੂਮਿ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Saahib singh ko sees katiyo su sadaa singh maar kai bhoomi giraayo |","meaning_en":"He cut off Sahib Singh's head and struck Sada Singh down to the ground;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਅਧੰਧਰ ਕੈ ਪੁਨਿ ਸਾਜਨ ਸਿੰਘ ਹਨ੍ਯੋ ਰਨ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sundar singh adhandhar kai puni saajan singh hanyo ran paayo |","meaning_en":"he cut Sundar Singh in half, then slew Sajan Singh in the battle;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਨ ਪਾਯੋ: read as 'in the battle'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਸਨ ਤੇ ਗਹਿ ਕੈ ਸਬਲੇਸ ਧਰਾ ਪਟਕਿਯੋ ਇਮ ਜੁਧ ਮਚਾਯੋ। ੧੨੭੬।","roman":"Kesan te gahi kai sables dharaa patkiyo im judh machaayo | 1276 |","meaning_en":"seizing Sabal Singh by the hair he dashed him to the ground: such was the battle he waged.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਬਲੇਸ: read as the name Sabal Singh."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1277],"number_text":"੧੨੭੭।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਪੁਨਿ ਹਨ੍ਯੋ ਰਨਿ ਸੈਨ ਸਿੰਘ ਹਤਿ ਦੀਨ।","roman":"Sakti singh puni hanyo rani sain singh hati deen |","meaning_en":"Then he slew Shakti Singh in the battle and killed Sain Singh;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ: read as a name, but a Shakti Singh (same spelling) fights on later in this section and is slain at its end; possibly a different king, or ਸਕਤਿ here means 'with might' ('then with might he slew...'); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਫਲ ਸਿੰਘ ਅਰਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਹਨਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਨਾਦ ਹਰਿ ਕੀਨ। ੧੨੭੭।","roman":"Saphal singh ari singh hani singh naad hari keen | 1277 |","meaning_en":"having slain Saphal Singh and Ari Singh, Krishna gave a lion's roar.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰਿ ਸਿੰਘ: read as a name; could mean 'the enemy'."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਸਵਛ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵਛ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Savachh singh baach","meaning_en":"Svachh Singh said:","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1278],"number_text":"੧੨੭੮।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਵਛ ਨਰੇਸ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਸਿਉ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਬਲ ਕੋਪਿ ਅਯੋਧਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Savachh nares kahiyo hari siu apune bal kopi ayodhan mai |","meaning_en":"King Svachh, angered on the battlefield, spoke to Krishna, trusting in his own strength:","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬ ਤੈ ਦਸ ਭੂਪ ਹਨੇ ਬਲਵੰਡ ਨ ਰੰਚਕ ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਕੀਯੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Ab tai das bhoop hane balvand na ranchak traas keeyo man mai |","meaning_en":"\"You have now slain ten kings, mighty one, but I have not the slightest fear in my mind.\"","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as Svachh Singh speaking of himself; could be 'and you felt no fear at all'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਕੀ ਓਰ ਤੇ ਤੀਰ ਚਲੈ ਬਰਖਾ ਜਿਮ ਸਾਵਨ ਕੇ ਘਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jadubeer kee or te teer chalai barkhaa jim saavan ke ghan mai |","meaning_en":"From the Yadav hero's side the arrows flew like rain from the clouds of Sawan;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sawan: the rainy month."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਪਉਨ ਕੇ ਜੋਰ ਲਗੇ ਨ ਟਰਿਓ ਗਿਰਿ ਜਿਉ ਥਿਰੁ ਠਾਢੋ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਰਨ ਮੈ।੧੨੭੮।","roman":"Sar paun ke jor lage na tario giri jiu thiru thaadho rahiyo ran mai | 1278 |","meaning_en":"though struck by arrows with the force of the wind, he did not move, but stood firm in the battle like a mountain.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1279],"number_text":"੧੨੭੯।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦੁ ਬੰਸਨ ਸੋ ਅਤਿ ਲਰਿਯੋ ਜਿਉ ਬਾਸਵ ਸਿਉ ਜੰਭ।","roman":"Jadu bansan so ati lariyo jiu baasav siu janbh |","meaning_en":"He fought hard against the Yadavs, as Jambh fought Indra;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਸਵ: Indra. Jambh: a demon."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਚਲ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਜਿਉ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਰਨ ਖੰਭ। ੧੨੭੯।","roman":"Achal rahiyo tih thaur nrip jiu ran mai ran khanbh | 1279 |","meaning_en":"the king stood immovable in that place, like a pillar on the battlefield.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1280],"number_text":"੧੨੮੦।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਨ ਹਲੈ ਗਿਰਿ ਕੰਚਨ ਕੋ ਅਤਿ ਹਾਥਨ ਕੋ ਬਲ ਕੋਊ ਕਰੈ।","roman":"Jiu na halai giri kanchan ko ati haathan ko bal ko'oo karai |","meaning_en":"As the golden mountain does not shake though someone pushes with all the strength of his hands,","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The golden mountain: Sumeru."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰੁ ਜਿਉ ਧ੍ਰੂ ਲੋਕ ਚਲੈ ਨ ਕਹੂੰ ਸਿਵ ਮੂਰਤਿ ਜਿਉ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਨ ਚਰੈ।","roman":"Aru jiu dhroo lok chalai na kahoon siv moorti jiu kabhoon na charai |","meaning_en":"and as the realm of Dhruv never moves, and as Shiva's image never stirs,","page":540,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Dhruv: the pole star."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰ ਜਿਉ ਨ ਸਤੀ ਸਤਿ ਛਾਡਿ ਪਤਿਬ੍ਰਤਿ ਜਿਉ ਸਿਧ ਜੋਗ ਮੈ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਧਰੈ।","roman":"Bar jiu na satee sati chhaadi patibrati jiu sidh jog mai dhyaan dharai |","meaning_en":"as a true wife does not abandon her virtue and faithfulness, as a siddha holds his meditation in yoga,","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਮ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਚਮੂੰ ਮਧਿ ਸਵਛ ਨਰੇਸ ਹਠੀ ਰਨ ਤੇ ਨਹੀ ਨੈਕੁ ਟਰੈ। ੧੨੮੦।","roman":"Tim syaam chamoon madhi savachh nares hathee ran te nahee naiku tarai | 1280 |","meaning_en":"so in the midst of Krishna's army the stubborn King Svachh did not move even a little from the battle.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","roman":"Kabitu","meaning_en":"Kabitt.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1281],"number_text":"੧੨੮੧।","page":540,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫੇਰਿ ਤਿਨ ਕੋਪਿ ਕੈ ਅਯੋਧਨ ਮੈ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹਿ","roman":"Pheri tin kopi kai ayodhan mai syaam kahi","meaning_en":"Then in his fury on the battlefield, says Shyam,","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Shyam: the poet's name."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਰ ਬਹੁ ਮਾਰੇ ਸਵਛ ਸਿੰਘ ਮਹਾ ਬਲ ਸੈ।","roman":"Beer bahu maare savachh singh mahaa bal sai |","meaning_en":"the very mighty Svachh Singh slew many warriors.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਰਥੀ ਸਤਿ ਮਹਾ ਰਥੀ ਜੁਗ ਸਤਿ","roman":"Ati rathee sati mahaa rathee jug sati","meaning_en":"A hundred atirathis, two hundred maharathis,","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Atirathi, maharathi: grades of chariot-warriors. ਜੁਗ ਸਤਿ: read as 'two hundred'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਹਾ ਸਿੰਧੁਰ ਹਜਾਰ ਹਨੇ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਕੇ ਦਲ ਸੈ।","roman":"Tahaa sindhur hajaar hane syaam joo ke dal sai |","meaning_en":"and a thousand elephants he slew there from Krishna's army.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਨੇ ਬਾਜ ਮਾਰੇ ਰਨਿ ਪੈਦਲ ਸੰਘਾਰੇ","roman":"Ghane baaj maare rani paidal sanghaare","meaning_en":"He killed many horses in the battle and destroyed the foot soldiers;","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਈ ਰੁਧਰ ਰੰਗੀਨ ਭੂਮਿ ਲਹਰੈ ਉਛਲ ਸੈ।","roman":"Bhaee rudhar rangeen bhoomi lahrai uchhal sai |","meaning_en":"the ground was dyed with blood, which surged in waves.","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਇਲ ਗਿਰੇ ਸੁ ਮਾਨੋ ਮਹਾ ਮਤਵਾਰੇ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ","roman":"Ghaail gire su maano mahaa matvaare hvai kai","meaning_en":"The wounded lay fallen as if heavily drunk,","page":540,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਏ ਰੂਮੀ ਤਰੈ ਲਾਲ ਡਾਰ ਕੈ ਅਤਲਸੈ। ੧੨੮੧।","roman":"Soe roomee tarai laal daar kai atalsai | 1281 |","meaning_en":"sleeping on red Rumi satin spread beneath them.","page":540,"flags":[{"code":"ੇੇ","reason":"same sign typed twice; written once (prints as one)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੂਮੀ...ਅਤਲਸੈ: 'satin from Rum (Turkey)'."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1282],"number_text":"੧੨੮੨।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਤ ਸੈਨ ਹਨਿ ਜਾਦਵੀ ਬਢਿਯੋ ਗਰਬ ਅਪਾਰ।","roman":"Bahut sain hani jaadvee badhiyo garab apaar |","meaning_en":"Having slain much of the Yadav army, his pride grew without limit;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨੁ ਉਤਾਰਿਯੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਬੋਲਿਓ ਕੋਪ ਹਕਾਰਿ। ੧੨੮੨।","roman":"Maanu utaariyo krisan prati bolio kop hakaari | 1282 |","meaning_en":"to bring down Krishna's pride he called out to him in anger:","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਨੁ ਉਤਾਰਿਯੋ: read as 'to humble (Krishna's) pride'; could also mean he cast off respect; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1283],"number_text":"੧੨੮੩।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਜੋ ਭੂਪ ਦਸ ਮਾਰੇ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਰਿਸਾਇ।","roman":"Kahaa bhayo jo bhoop das maare syaam risaai |","meaning_en":"\"What of it if Krishna in his anger has killed ten kings?","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਬਨ ਤਿਨ ਭਛ ਕਰ ਲਰੇ ਨ ਹਰਿ ਸਮੁਹਾਇ। ੧੨੮੩।","roman":"Jiu mrig ban tin bhachh kar lare na hari samuhaai | 1283 |","meaning_en":"They were like deer that graze in the forest and do not face the lion in a fight.\"","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰਿ: here read as 'lion' (a play on Hari)."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1284],"number_text":"੧੨੮੪।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਿਪੁ ਕੇ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਨੰਤ ਹੀ ਬੋਲੇ ਹਰਿ ਮੁਸਕਾਇ।","roman":"Ripu ke bachan sunant hee bole hari muskaai |","meaning_en":"As soon as he heard the enemy's words, Krishna smiled and said,","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਵਛ ਸਿੰਘ ਤੁਅ ਮਾਰਿ ਹੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੀ ਨਯਾਇ। ੧੨੮੪।","roman":"Savachh singh tua maari ho syaar singh kee nayaai | 1284 |","meaning_en":"\"Svachh Singh, I will kill you as a lion kills a jackal.\"","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1285],"number_text":"੧੨੮੫।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿੰਘ ਨਿਹਾਰ ਕੈ ਜਿਉ ਸਰਦੂਲ ਘਨੋ ਬਲ ਕੈ ਰਿਸ ਸਾਥਿ ਤਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Singh nihaar kai jiu sardool ghano bal kai ris saathi tachaayo |","meaning_en":"As a lion, seeing another lion, burns with great strength and fury,","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿੰਘ...ਸਰਦੂਲ: both mean lion; read as one lion seeing another; ਸਰਦੂਲ could also be a tiger; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਗਜਰਾਜ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਬਨ ਮੈ ਮ੍ਰਿਗਰਾਜ ਮਨੋ ਅਤਿ ਕੋਪ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jiu gajraaj lakhiyo ban mai mrigraaj mano ati kop badhaayo |","meaning_en":"as the king of beasts, seeing a mighty elephant in the forest, swells with anger,","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਚਿਤਵਾ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਪੇਖ ਕੈ ਦਉਰਤ ਸਵਛ ਨਰੇਸ ਪੈ ਤਿਉ ਹਰਿ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jiu chitvaa mrig pekh kai daurat savachh nares pai tiu hari dhaayo |","meaning_en":"as a cheetah runs on seeing a deer, so Krishna rushed at King Svachh;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਉਨ ਕੇ ਗਉਨ ਤੇ ਆਗੇ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਰਥੁ ਦਾਰੁਕ ਐਸੇ ਧਵਾਯੋ। ੧੨੮੫।","roman":"Paun ke gaun te aage chaliyo hari ko rathu daaruk aise dhavaayo | 1285 |","meaning_en":"Daruk drove Krishna's chariot so that it went faster than the wind.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Daruk: Krishna's charioteer."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1286],"number_text":"੧੨੮੬।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਤ ਤੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸਵਛ ਭਯੋ ਸਮੁਹੇ ਇਤ ਤੇ ਸੁ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਬਲ ਭਈਯਾ।","roman":"Ut te nrip savachh bhayo samuhe it te su chaliyo ris kai bal bhaeeyaa |","meaning_en":"From there King Svachh came face to face; from here Balram's brother advanced in anger.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲ ਭਈਯਾ: read as 'brother of Bal(ram)', i.e. Krishna."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਲਰੇ ਦੋਊ ਆਪਸਿ ਮੈ ਬਰ ਜੁਧੁ ਕਰਈਯਾ।","roman":"Baan kamaan kripaan lare do'oo aapsi mai bar judhu karaeeyaa |","meaning_en":"Both fought each other with bows, arrows and swords, waging a great battle;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰ ਹੀ ਮਾਰ ਪੁਕਾਰਿ ਅਰੇ ਨ ਟਰੇ ਰਨ ਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਧੀਰ ਧਰਈਯਾ।","roman":"Maar hee maar pukaari are na tare ran te ati dheer dharaeeyaa |","meaning_en":"crying \"Kill! Kill!\" they stood firm, and did not turn from the field, holding great steadfastness.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਤੇ ਰਾਮ ਤੇ ਜਾਦਵ ਤੇ ਨ ਡਰਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਲਰਿਯੋ ਬਰ ਬੀਰ ਲਰਈਯਾ। ੧੨੮੬।","roman":"Syaam te raam te jaadav te na dariyo su lariyo bar beer laraeeyaa | 1286 |","meaning_en":"He did not fear Krishna, Balram or the Yadavs; he fought like a great warrior.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1287],"number_text":"੧੨੮੭।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਿਕ ਜੁਧੁ ਜਬ ਤਿਨ ਕੀਯੋ ਤਬ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਪਤਿ ਕਾ ਕੀਨ।","roman":"Adhik judhu jab tin keeyo tab brij pati kaa keen |","meaning_en":"When he had fought a great deal, what did the Lord of Braj do?","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੜਗ ਧਾਰਿ ਸਿਰ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਕੋ ਮਾਰਿ ਜੁਦਾ ਕਰਿ ਦੀਨ। ੧੨੮੭।","roman":"Kharag dhaari sir satr ko maari judaa kari deen | 1287 |","meaning_en":"With the edge of his sword he struck the enemy's head and severed it.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1288],"number_text":"੧੨੮੮।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਵਛ ਸਿੰਘ ਜਬ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ ਸਮਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੀਓ ਕੋਪ।","roman":"Savachh singh jab maariyo samar singh keeo kop |","meaning_en":"When Svachh Singh was killed, Samar Singh grew angry;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹ ਭਾਜਿਯੋ ਲਖਿ ਸਮਰ ਕੋ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਦਿੜ ਪਗੁ ਰੋਪਿ। ੧੨੮੮।","roman":"Nah bhaajiyo lakhi samar ko rahiyo su dir pagu ropi | 1288 |","meaning_en":"seeing the battle he did not flee, but stood with his feet firmly planted.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1289],"number_text":"੧੨੮੯।","page":541,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਸ ਕ ਬੀਰ ਬਲੀ ਅਸਿ ਲੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਭਟ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਕੇ ਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Ros ka beer balee asi lai ati hee bhat sree jadubeer ke maare |","meaning_en":"In fury the mighty warrior took his sword and slew many of the Yadav hero's soldiers;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੋਸ ਕ: printed so; read as ਰੋਸ ਕੈ ('in anger')."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਕਿਤੇ ਗਿਰੇ ਘਾਇਲ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕਿਤਨੇ ਰਨ ਭੂਮਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਪਧਾਰੇ।","roman":"Aur kite gire ghaail hvai kitne ran bhoomi nihaari padhaare |","meaning_en":"many others fell wounded, and many, seeing the battlefield, went away.","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਪੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਮਰੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਹਮ ਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Syaam joo pai ih bhaati kahiyo samres balee tih te ham haare |","meaning_en":"They said to Krishna thus: \"Mighty Samar Singh has defeated us;","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਮਰੇਸ: Samar Singh."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਸੀ ਮੈ ਜਿਉ ਕਲਵਤ੍ਰ ਵਹੈ ਤਿਮ ਬੀਰਨ ਚੀਰ ਕੇ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰੇ। ੧੨੮੯।","roman":"Kaasee mai jiu kalvatr vahai tim beeran cheer ke dvai kari daare | 1289 |","meaning_en":"as the saw works at Kashi, so he has split warriors in two.\"","page":541,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲਵਤ੍ਰ: the saw at Kashi (Varanasi) by which devotees were said to give their lives."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1290],"number_text":"੧੨੯੦।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੋਲਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਦਲ ਮੈ ਭਟ ਹੈ ਕੋਊ ਜੋ ਅਰਿ ਸੰਗ ਲਰੈ।","roman":"Boli kahiyo hari joo dal mai bhat hai ko'oo jo ari sang larai |","meaning_en":"Krishna called out in the army, \"Is there any warrior who will fight the enemy,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਹ ਕੋ ਬਹੁ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਹੈ ਤਨ ਮੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਉਹਿ ਊਪਰ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਕਰੈ।","roman":"Uh ko bahu asatr sahai tan mai apne uhi oopar sasatr karai |","meaning_en":"who will bear his many weapons on his body and strike him with his own weapons?\"","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਜ ਪਾਨ ਮੈ ਪਾਨ ਧਰੇ ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁ ਕੋਇ ਨ ਬੀਰਨ ਲਾਜ ਧਰੈ।","roman":"Nij paan mai paan dhare ghan syaam su koi na beeran laaj dharai |","meaning_en":"Krishna held a betel leaf in his hand, but none of the warriors stood up for honour.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Holding out betel (paan): a custom by which whoever takes it accepts the challenge. ਲਾਜ ਧਰੈ: read as 'take up the honour'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਨ ਮੈ ਜਸ ਕੋ ਸੋਊ ਟੀਕੋ ਲਹੈ ਸਮਰੇਸ ਕੇ ਜੁਧ ਤੇ ਨਾਹਿ ਟਰੈ। ੧੨੯੦।","roman":"Ran mai jas ko so'oo teeko lahai samres ke judh te naahi tarai | 1290 |","meaning_en":"\"He will win the mark of glory in battle who does not turn back from fighting Samar Singh.\"","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਟੀਕੋ: 'tilak, mark of honour'."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1291],"number_text":"੧੨੯੧।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਤੁ ਜੁਧੁ ਸੁਭਟਨਿ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਕਹਾ ਕਰੈ ਬਲਵਾਨ।","roman":"Bahutu judhu subhatni kariyo kahaa karai balvaan |","meaning_en":"Good warriors had fought much, but what could they do against the mighty one?","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਹਵ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਲੀ ਹੁਤੋ ਮਾਗ ਲੀਏ ਤਿਹ ਪਾਨ। ੧੨੯੧।","roman":"Aahav singh balee huto maag lee'e tih paan | 1291 |","meaning_en":"Aahav Singh was a strong warrior; he asked for the betel leaf.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1292],"number_text":"੧੨੯੨।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਊ ਪ੍ਰਸਨ ਇਹ ਠਾ ਕਰੈ ਕਿਉ ਨ ਲਰੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਰਾਜ।","roman":"Ko'oo prasan ih thaa karai kiu na larai brij raaj |","meaning_en":"Someone may ask here, \"Why does the Lord of Braj not fight?\"","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਹ ਉਤਰ ਹੈ ਤਾਹਿ ਕੋ ਕਉਤੁਕ ਦੇਖਨ ਕਾਜ। ੧੨੯੨।","roman":"Yah utar hai taahi ko kautuk dekhan kaaj | 1292 |","meaning_en":"The answer to him is this: in order to watch the spectacle.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1293],"number_text":"੧੨੯੩।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਹਵ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਲੀ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਭਟ ਸੋ ਤਿਹ ਉਪਰ ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aahav singh balee hari ko bhat so tih upar kop kai dhaayo |","meaning_en":"Aahav Singh, Krishna's mighty warrior, rushed at him in anger;","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਘਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਹਠੀ ਹਠਿ ਸਿਉ ਨ ਹਟਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਤਹਾ ਅਤਿ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sanghar singh hathee hathi siu na hatiyo su tahaa ati judhu machaayo |","meaning_en":"the stubborn Sanghar Singh did not budge from his resolve, and there he waged a fierce battle.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਘਰ ਸਿੰਘ: read as another name for Samar Singh (both 'samar' and 'sanghar' mean battle)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਹਵ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੋ ਸੰਘਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਮਹਾ ਅਸਿ ਲੈ ਸਿਰ ਕਾਟਿ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aahav singh ko sanghar singh mahaa asi lai sir kaati giraayo |","meaning_en":"The great Sanghar Singh took his sword and cut off Aahav Singh's head;","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਧਰਿ ਪੈ ਧਰ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਬਜ੍ਰ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਭੂਅ ਕੰਪੁ ਜਨਾਯੋ। ੧੨੯੩।","roman":"Aise pariyo dhari pai dhar maanhu bajr pariyo bhooa kanpu janaayo | 1293 |","meaning_en":"his body fell on the ground as if a thunderbolt had struck, and the earth was felt to quake.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","roman":"Kabitu","meaning_en":"Kabitt.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1294],"number_text":"੧੨੯੪।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਪ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਸਿੰਘ ਠਾਢੋ ਹੁਤੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਤੀਰ","roman":"Bhoop anrudh singh thaadho huto syaam teer","meaning_en":"King Anrudh Singh was standing near Krishna;","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਬਿਲੋਕ ਕੈ ਨਿਕਟਿ ਬੋਲਿ ਲਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Hari joo bilok kai nikti boli layo hai |","meaning_en":"seeing him, Krishna called him close.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੀਨੋ ਸਨਮਾਨ ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਜਾਹੁ ਤੁਮ","roman":"Keeno sanmaan ghan syaam kahiyo jaahu tum","meaning_en":"Krishna did him honour and said, \"Go\";","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਥਹਿ ਧਵਾਇ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਰਨ ਮਾਝ ਗਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Rathhi dhavaai chaliyo ran maajh gayo hai |","meaning_en":"driving his chariot he set off and went into the midst of the battle.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੀਰ ਤਰਵਾਰਨ ਕੋ ਸੈਥੀ ਜਮਦਾਰਨ ਕੋ","roman":"Teer tarvaaran ko saithee jamdaaran ko","meaning_en":"With arrows and swords, with lances and daggers,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੈਥੀ: a lance; ਜਮਦਾਰ: a dagger."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟਕਾ ਦੁਇ ਤਿਹੀ ਠਉਰ ਮਹਾ ਜੁਧੁ ਭਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Ghatkaa dui tihee thaur mahaa judhu bhayo hai |","meaning_en":"for two gharis a great battle was fought in that place.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਸਿੰਘ ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਕੋ ਸਿਚਾਨੋ ਜੈਸੇ ਚਿਰੀਆ ਕੋ","roman":"Jaise singh mrig ko sichaano jaise chireeaa ko","meaning_en":"As a lion kills a deer, as a hawk kills a sparrow,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈਸੇ ਹਰਿ ਬੀਰ ਕੋ ਸਮਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਹਯੋ ਹੈ। ੧੨੯੪।","roman":"Taise hari beer ko samar singh hayo hai | 1294 |","meaning_en":"so Samar Singh slew Krishna's warrior.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1295],"number_text":"੧੨੯੫।","page":542,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਕੋਊ ਅਉਖਦਿ ਕੇ ਬਲ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ","roman":"Jaise ko'oo aukhdi ke bal kabi syaam kahai","meaning_en":"As, says the poet Shyam, by the power of medicine","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੂਰ ਕਰੇ ਸਤਿ ਬੈਦ ਰੋਗ ਸੰਨਿਪਾਤ ਕੋ।","roman":"Door kare sati baid rog sannipaat ko |","meaning_en":"a true physician removes the disease of sannipat;","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sannipat: a severe fever."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਕੋਊ ਸੁਕਬਿ ਕੁਕਬਿ ਕੇ ਕਬਿਤ ਸੁਨਿ","roman":"Jaise ko'oo sukbi kukbi ke kabit suni","meaning_en":"as a good poet, hearing a bad poet's verses","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭਾ ਬੀਚ ਦੂਖਿ ਕਰਿ ਮਾਨਤ ਨ ਬਾਤ ਕੋ।","roman":"Sabhaa beech dookhi kari maanat na baat ko |","meaning_en":"in the assembly, finds fault and does not accept a word of them;","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਸਿੰਘ ਨਾਗ ਕੋ ਹਨਤ ਜਲ ਆਗ ਕੋ","roman":"Jaise singh naag ko hanat jal aag ko","meaning_en":"as a lion kills an elephant, as water quenches fire,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਾਗ: read as 'elephant'; could mean 'snake'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਲ ਸੁਰ ਰਾਗ ਕੋ ਸਚਿੰਤ ਨਰ ਗਾਤ ਕੋ।","roman":"Amal sur raag ko sachint nar gaat ko |","meaning_en":"as intoxication spoils the notes of a raga, as worry wastes a man's body,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਮਲ ਸੁਰ ਰਾਗ ਕੋ ਸਚਿੰਤ ਨਰ ਗਾਤ ਕੋ: obscure; read as 'intoxication (amal) ruins the melody, anxiety ruins the body'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈਸੇ ਤਤਕਾਲ ਹਰਿ ਬੀਰ ਮਾਰ ਡਾਰਿਯੋ","roman":"Taise tatkaal hari beer maar daariyo","meaning_en":"so at once he struck down Krishna's warrior,","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਲੋਭ ਹੂੰ ਤੇ ਮਹਾ ਗੁਨਿ ਨਾਸੈ ਤਮ ਪ੍ਰਾਤ ਕੋ। ੧੨੯੫।","roman":"Jaise lobh hoon te mahaa guni naasai tam praat ko | 1295 |","meaning_en":"as great virtue is destroyed by greed, and as morning destroys the darkness.","page":542,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1296],"number_text":"੧੨੯੬।","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਰਭਦ੍ਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਾਸੁਦੇਵ ਸਿੰਘ ਬੀਰ ਸਿੰਘ","roman":"Beerbhadr singh baasudev singh beer singh","meaning_en":"Birbhadra Singh, Basudev Singh, Bir Singh","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਲ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੋਪ ਕਰਿ ਅਰਿ ਸਮੁਹੇ ਭਏ।","roman":"Bal singh kop kari ari samuhe bhae |","meaning_en":"and Bal Singh in anger came face to face with the enemy.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਮਰ ਕੇ ਬੀਚ ਜਹਾ ਠਾਢੋ ਹੈ ਸਮਰ ਸਿੰਘ","roman":"Samar ke beech jahaa thaadho hai samar singh","meaning_en":"There in the battle where Samar Singh stood,","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੋ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਰੂਪ ਪਾਵਕ ਸੇ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਗਏ।","roman":"Taahee ko nihaari roop paavak se hvai gae |","meaning_en":"seeing him they became like fire.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਯੁਧ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਲੀਨੇ ਜੁਧ ਮੈ ਸਬੈ ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨੇ","roman":"Aayudh sanbhaari leene judh mai sabai prabeene","meaning_en":"They took up their weapons, all skilled in war;","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਕੇ ਬੀਰ ਚਾਰੋ ਓਰ ਹੂੰ ਤੇ ਆ ਖਏ।","roman":"Syaam joo ke beer chaaro or hoon te aa khae |","meaning_en":"Krishna's warriors came and clashed with him from all four sides.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆ ਖਏ: read as 'came and clashed'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਸਮੇ ਬਲਵਾਨ ਤਾਨ ਕੇ ਕਮਾਨ ਬਾਨ","roman":"Taahee same balvaan taan ke kamaan baan","meaning_en":"At that time the mighty one drew his bow and arrows","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਕੇ ਮਾਰਿ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਲਏ। ੧੨੯੬।","roman":"Chaaro nrip hari joo ke maari chhin mai lae | 1296 |","meaning_en":"and in an instant slew all four of Krishna's kings.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach","meaning_en":"Krishna said:","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1297],"number_text":"੧੨੯੭","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਚਾਰੋ ਈ ਬੀਰ ਹਨੇ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਤਬ ਅਉਰਨ ਸਿਉ ਹਰਿ ਯੌ ਉਚਰੈ।","roman":"Jab chaaro ee beer hane ran mai tab auran siu hari yau uchrai |","meaning_en":"When all four warriors had been slain in the battle, Krishna spoke thus to the others:","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬ ਕੋ ਭਟ ਹੈ ਹਮਰੇ ਦਲ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਜੁਧ ਕਰੈ।","roman":"Ab ko bhat hai hamre dal mai ih saamuhe jaai kai judh karai |","meaning_en":"\"Now who is the warrior in our army who will go before him and fight,","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਬਲਵਾਨ ਸੋ ਧਾਇ ਕੈ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਘਾਇ ਕਰੈ ਸੁ ਲਰੈ ਨ ਡਰੈ।","roman":"Ati hee balvaan so dhaai kai jaai kai ghaai karai su larai na darai |","meaning_en":"who will rush at this very mighty one, go and strike him, and fight without fear?\"","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਸਿਉ ਇਮ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਪੁਕਾਰਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਕੋਊ ਹੈ ਅਰਿ ਕੋ ਬਿਨੁ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਕਰੈ। ੧੨੯੭","roman":"Sab siu im syaam pukaari kahiyo ko'oo hai ari ko binu praan karai | 1297","meaning_en":"Krishna called out thus to all: \"Is there anyone who will take the enemy's life?\"","page":543,"flags":[{"code":"print","reason":"verse number printed without its closing danda"}],"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1298],"number_text":"੧੨੯੮।","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਛਸ ਹੋ ਇਕ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੀ ਓਰ ਸੋਊ ਚਲ ਕੈ ਅਰਿ ਓਰ ਪਧਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Raachhas ho ik syaam kee or so'oo chal kai ari or padhaariyo |","meaning_en":"There was a demon on Krishna's side; he set out and went towards the enemy.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰ�ਰ ਧੁਜਾ ਤਿਹ ਨਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਜਗ ਸੋ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Kra(?)ra dhujaa tih naam kahai jag so tih so ih bhaati uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"The world called him Krur Dhuja; he spoke to him thus:","page":543,"flags":[{"code":"0xad","reason":"unresolved: draws an empty box in the PDF itself: the source font lacks this glyph"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕ੍ਰ�ਰ: printed with an unreadable character; read as ਕ੍ਰੂਰ (Krur)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਤ ਹੋ ਰੇ ਸੰਭਾਰੁ ਅਬੈ ਕਰਿ ਯਾ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਧਨੁ ਬਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Maarat ho re sanbhaaru abai kari yaa bateeyaa dhanu baan sanbhaariyo |","meaning_en":"\"I am about to strike you; be on your guard now!\" Saying these words, he took up bow and arrows.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਸਮਰੇਸ ਕੋ ਬਾਨ ਹਨਿਯੋ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਠਉਰ ਮਨੋ ਕਈ ਦਿਵਸ ਕੋ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ। ੧੨੯੮।","roman":"Taa samres ko baan haniyo rahiyo thaur mano kaee divas ko maariyo | 1298 |","meaning_en":"He struck Samar Singh with an arrow, and he lay on that spot as if he had been killed days before.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1299],"number_text":"੧੨੯੯।","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰ�ਰ ਧੁਜਾ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਹਨ੍ਯੋ ਸਮਰ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੋ ਕੋਪਿ।","roman":"Kra(?)ra dhujaa ran mai hanyo samar singh ko kopi |","meaning_en":"Krur Dhuja in his anger slew Samar Singh in the battle;","page":543,"flags":[{"code":"0xad","reason":"unresolved: draws an empty box in the PDF itself: the source font lacks this glyph"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕ੍ਰ�ਰ: printed with an unreadable character; read as ਕ੍ਰੂਰ (Krur)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੇ ਬਧਨ ਕੋ ਬਹੁਰ ਰਹਿਓ ਪਗੁ ਰੋਪਿ। ੧੨੯੯।","roman":"Sakti singh ke badhan ko bahur rahio pagu ropi | 1299 |","meaning_en":"then he stood with feet planted firm to kill Shakti Singh.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਧੁਜ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਧੁਜ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kroor dhuj baach","meaning_en":"Krur Dhuj said:","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਤੁ","roman":"Kabitu","meaning_en":"Kabitt.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1300],"number_text":"੧੩੦੦।","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰਿ ਸੋ ਦਿਖਾਈ ਦੇਤ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਧੁਜ ਆਹਵ ਮੈ","roman":"Giri so dikhaaee det kroor dhuj aahav mai","meaning_en":"Krur Dhuj looks like a mountain on the battlefield;","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੈ ਕਬਿ ਰਾਮ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਬਧ ਕੋ ਚਹਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kahai kabi raam satr badh ko chahat hai |","meaning_en":"says the poet Ram, he wants to kill the enemy.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Ram: the poet's name."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਰੇ ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ ਜਿਉ ਸਮਰ ਸਿੰਘ","roman":"Suni re sakti singh maariyo jiu samar singh","meaning_en":"\"Listen, Shakti Singh: as I have killed Samar Singh,","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈਸੇ ਹਉ ਹਨਿ ਹੋ ਤੂ ਹਮ ਸੋ ਖਹਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Taise hau hani ho too ham so khahat hai |","meaning_en":"so I will kill you, since you are clashing with me.\"","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿ ਗਦਾ ਗਹਿ ਬੜੇ ਬ੍ਰਿਛ ਕੇ ਸਮਾਨ","roman":"Aise kahi gadaa gahi bare brichh ke samaan","meaning_en":"Saying this he took up a mace like a great tree,","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੀਨ ਅਸਿ ਪਾਨਿ ਅਉਰ ਸਸਤ੍ਰਨਿ ਸਹਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Leen asi paani aur sastrani sahat hai |","meaning_en":"and took a sword in his hand along with other weapons.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਰੋ ਪੁਕਾਰਿ ਦੈਤ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਹੈ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ","roman":"Bahuro pukaari dait kahiyo hai nihaari nrip","meaning_en":"Again the demon called out, looking at the king,","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਮੈ ਕੋਊ ਘਰੀ ਪਲ ਜੀਵਨ ਰਹਤ ਹੈ। ੧੩੦੦।","roman":"To mai ko'oo gharee pal jeevan rahat hai | 1300 |","meaning_en":"\"There is only a ghari or a moment of life left in you.\"","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1301],"number_text":"੧੩੦੧।","page":543,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਸੁਨਿ ਅਰਿ ਸਬਦਿ ਬੋਲਿਯੋ ਕੋਪੁ ਬਢਾਇ।","roman":"Sakti singh suni ari sabdi boliyo kopu badhaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing the enemy's words, Shakti Singh spoke with mounting anger:","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨਤ ਹੋ ਘਨ ਕ੍ਵਾਰ ਕੋ ਗਰਜਤ ਬਰਸਿ ਨ ਆਇ। ੧੩੦੧।","roman":"Jaanat ho ghan kvaar ko garjat barsi na aai | 1301 |","meaning_en":"\"I know you: the cloud of Kuar thunders but brings no rain.\"","page":543,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Kuar (Assu): the autumn month after the rains."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1302],"number_text":"੧੩੦੨।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਤਿਹ ਬਾਤ ਨਿਸਾਚਾਰ ਜੀ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਅਤਿ ਕੋਪ ਭਰਿਓ।","roman":"Yau suni kai tih baat nisaachaar jee apune ati kop bhario |","meaning_en":"Hearing his words, the night-wanderer was filled with great anger in his heart;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸਾਚਾਰ: printed so; read as ਨਿਸਾਚਰ ('night-wanderer', demon)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਿ ਲੈ ਤਿਹ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਆਇ ਅਰਿਯੋ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਨਹੀ ਨੈਕੁ ਡਰਿਓ।","roman":"Asi lai tih saamuhe aai ariyo saktes balee nahee naiku dario |","meaning_en":"sword in hand he came and stood firm before him, but mighty Shakti Singh was not the least afraid.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਕਤੇਸ: Shakti Singh."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁ ਜੁਧ ਕੈ ਅੰਤਰਿ ਧਿਆਨ ਭਯੋ ਨਭਿ ਮੈ ਪ੍ਰਗਟਿਯੋ ਤੇ ਉਚਰਿਓ।","roman":"Bahu judh kai antri dhiaan bhayo nabhi mai pragtiyo te uchrio |","meaning_en":"After much fighting he vanished, and appearing in the sky he called out,","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬ ਤੋਹਿ ਸੰਘਾਰਿਤ ਹੋ ਪਲ ਮੈ ਧਨੁ ਬਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਰ ਕੈ ਪਾਨਿ ਧਰਿਓ। ੧੩੦੨।","roman":"Ab tohi sanghaarit ho pal mai dhanu baan sanbhaar kai paani dhario | 1302 |","meaning_en":"\"Now I will destroy you in a moment!\" and he took bow and arrows in his hand.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1303],"number_text":"੧੩੦੩","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨਨ ਕੀ ਬਰਖਾ ਕਰਤ ਨਭ ਤੇ ਉਤਰਿਯੋ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ।","roman":"Baanan kee barkhaa karat nabh te utriyo kroor |","meaning_en":"Raining arrows, Krur came down from the sky;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਆਯੋ ਰਨ ਭੂਮਿ ਮੈ ਅਧਿਕ ਲਰਿਯੋ ਬਰ ਸੂਰ। ੧੩੦੩","roman":"Puni aayo ran bhoomi mai adhik lariyo bar soor | 1303","meaning_en":"he came again onto the battlefield, and the great warrior fought hard.","page":544,"flags":[{"code":"print","reason":"verse number printed without its closing danda"}],"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1304],"number_text":"੧੩੦੪।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਰਨ ਮਾਰ ਕੈ ਦੈਤ ਬਲੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਹਰਖਿਓ ਹੈ।","roman":"Beeran maar kai dait balee apne chit mai ati hee harkhio hai |","meaning_en":"Having slain warriors, the mighty demon rejoiced greatly in his heart;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੀ ਤਜਿ ਸੰਕ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਭਯੋ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਸੰਘਾਰਬੇ ਕੋ ਸਰਖਿਓ ਹੈ।","roman":"Hee taji sank nisank bhayo saktes sanghaarbe ko sarkhio hai |","meaning_en":"casting off all doubt, he became fearless and pressed forward to destroy Shakti Singh.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਰਖਿਓ: read as 'pressed forward, moved'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਚਪਲਾ ਚਮਕੈ ਬਰਿ ਚਾਪ ਲੀਯੋ ਕਰ ਮੈ ਕਰਖਿਓ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jiu chaplaa chamkai bari chaap leeyo kar mai karkhio hai |","meaning_en":"Like lightning flashing, he took his fine bow in hand and drew it;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੇਘ ਪਰੇ ਬਰ ਬੂੰਦਨ ਜਿਉ ਸਰ ਜਾਲ ਕਰਾਲਨਿ ਤਿਉ ਬਰਖਿਓ ਹੈ। ੧੩੦੪।","roman":"Megh pare bar boondan jiu sar jaal karaalni tiu barkhio hai | 1304 |","meaning_en":"as clouds pour down big drops, so he rained terrible nets of arrows.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1305],"number_text":"੧੩੦੫।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਗ ਨ ਟਰਿਓ ਬਰ ਬੀਰ ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਧੁਜ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ ਤੇ।","roman":"Pag na tario bar beer sakti singh dhuj kroor te |","meaning_en":"The great warrior Shakti Singh did not move a step before Krur Dhuj;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਚਲ ਰਹਿਓ ਰਨ ਧੀਰ ਜਿਉ ਅੰਗਦ ਰਾਵਨ ਸਭਾ। ੧੩੦੫।","roman":"Achal rahio ran dheer jiu angad raavan sabhaa | 1305 |","meaning_en":"steadfast in battle he stayed immovable, like Angad in Ravan's court.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Angad: in the Ramayan, he planted his foot in Ravan's court and no one could move it."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1306],"number_text":"੧੩੦੬।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜਤ ਨਾਹਿਨ ਆਹਵ ਤੇ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਮਹਾ ਬਲਵੰਤ ਸੰਭਾਰਿਓ।","roman":"Bhaajat naahin aahav te saktes mahaa balvant sanbhaario |","meaning_en":"The very mighty Shakti Singh did not flee the battle, but kept his guard;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਲ ਜਿਤੋ ਅਰਿ ਕੇ ਸਰ ਕੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਅਗਨਾਯੁਧ ਸਾਥ ਪ੍ਰਜਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Jaal jito ari ke sar ko tab hee agnaayudh saath prajaariyo |","meaning_en":"the whole net of the enemy's arrows he then burnt with the fire-weapon.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਗਨਾਯੁਧ: the fire missile (agneyastra)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਨਿ ਲਯੋ ਧਨੁ ਬਾਨ ਰਿਸਾਇ ਕੈ ਕ੍ਰੂ ਧੁਜਾ ਸਿਰ ਕਾਟਿ ਉਤਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Paani layo dhanu baan risaai kai kroo dhujaa sir kaati utaariyo |","meaning_en":"In fury he took bow and arrows in hand and cut off Krur Dhuja's head;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕ੍ਰੂ ਧੁਜਾ: printed so; read as Krur Dhuja."},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਹਨ੍ਯੋ ਰਿਪੁ ਜਿਉ ਮਘਵਾ ਬਲ ਕੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਤਰਾਸੁਰ ਦੈਤ ਸੰਘਾਰਿਓ। ੧੩੦੬।","roman":"Aise hanyo ripu jiu maghvaa bal kai britraasur dait sanghaario | 1306 |","meaning_en":"he slew the enemy as Indra by his might destroyed the demon Vritrasur.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1307],"number_text":"੧੩੦੭।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਜਬ ਕ੍ਰੂਰਧੁਜ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ ਭੂਮਿ ਗਿਰਾਇ।","roman":"Sakti singh jab kroordhuj maariyo bhoomi giraai |","meaning_en":"When Shakti Singh had killed Krur Dhuj and felled him to the ground,","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਬਰਖਾ ਰਿਤੁ ਕੇ ਸਮੈ ਦਉਰ ਪਰੇ ਅਰਿਰਾਇ। ੧੩੦੭।","roman":"Jiu barkhaa ritu ke samai daur pare ariraai | 1307 |","meaning_en":"the enemies rushed in, roaring, like clouds in the rainy season.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰਿਰਾਇ: read as 'roaring' (ਅਰਰਾਇ); could mean 'enemy kings'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1308],"number_text":"੧੩੦੮।","page":544,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਕਧੁਜਾ ਨਿਜ ਭ੍ਰਾਤ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਹਨ੍ਯੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਵਹੁ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaakdhujaa nij bhraat nihaari hanyo tab hee ris kai vahu dhaayo |","meaning_en":"Kak Dhuja, seeing his brother slain, at once rushed forward in anger;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਤ ਕੀਏ ਕਈ ਜੋਜਨ ਲਉ ਗਿਰਿ ਸੋ ਤਿਹ ਆਪਨੋ ਰੂਪ ਬਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Daat kee'e kaee jojan lau giri so tih aapno roop banaayo |","meaning_en":"he made his teeth many yojans long and made his form like a mountain;","page":544,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Yojan: a measure of distance of several miles."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਮ ਕੀਏ ਤਰੁ ਸੇ ਤਨ ਮੈ ਕਰਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਰਨਿ ਭੂਮਹਿ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Rom kee'e taru se tan mai kari aayudh lai rani bhoomhi aayo |","meaning_en":"he made the hairs on his body like trees, and came to the battlefield with weapons in hand.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਤਨ੍ਯੋ ਕਰਿ ਚਾਪ ਸੁ ਏਕ ਹੀ ਬਾਨ ਸਿਉ ਮਾਰਿ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ। ੧੩੦੮।","roman":"Sree saktes tanyo kari chaap su ek hee baan siu maari giraayo | 1308 |","meaning_en":"Shakti Singh drew his bow and felled him with a single arrow.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1309],"number_text":"੧੩੦੯।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੈਤ ਚਮੂੰ ਪਤਿ ਠਾਢੋ ਹੁਤੋ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਬਰ ਕੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਊਪਰਿ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Dait chamoon pati thaadho huto tih ko bar kai nrip oopri dhaayo |","meaning_en":"The commander of the demon army was standing there; for his sake he rushed forcefully at the king.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਬਰ ਕੈ: read as 'on his account / with force'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਛਸ ਸੈਨ ਅਛੂਹਨਿ ਲੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਕੋਪ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Raachhas sain achhoohni lai apne man mai ati kop badhaayo |","meaning_en":"Taking an akshauhini of the demon army, he swelled with great anger in his heart;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਬਨਾਇ ਚਢਿਯੋ ਰਨ ਕੋ ਤਿਹ ਆਪਨ ਨਾਮੁ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਕਹਾਯੋ।","roman":"Baan banaai chadhiyo ran ko tih aapan naamu kuroop kahaayo |","meaning_en":"arrayed for war he went into battle; he called himself by the name Kuroop.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਨ ਬਨਾਇ: read as 'putting on battle dress' (baana); could mean 'readying arrows'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਅਰਿ ਕੇ ਬਧ ਕੋ ਮਨੋ ਸਾਵਨ ਕੋ ਉਨਏ ਘਨੁ ਆਯੋ। ੧੩੦੯।","roman":"Aise chaliyo ari ke badh ko mano saavan ko unae ghanu aayo | 1309 |","meaning_en":"He set out to kill the enemy like a cloud of Sawan gathering and coming on.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1310],"number_text":"੧੩੧੦।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੇਰਿ ਚਮੂੰ ਬਹੁ ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੀ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਮਨਿ ਰੋਸ ਭਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Heri chamoon bahu satran kee saktes balee mani ros bhayo hai |","meaning_en":"Seeing the great army of the enemy, mighty Shakti Singh grew angry at heart;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧੀਰਜ ਬਾਧਿ ਅਯੋਧਨ ਮਾਝਿ ਸਰਾਸਨਿ ਬਾਨ ਸੁ ਪਾਨਿ ਲਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Dheeraj baadhi ayodhan maajhi saraasni baan su paani layo hai |","meaning_en":"holding firm in the midst of the battle, he took bow and arrows in hand;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਸਬੈ ਤਜਿ ਕੈ ਲਜਿ ਕੈ ਅਰਿ ਕੇ ਦਲ ਕੇ ਸਮੁਹੇ ਸੁ ਗਯੋ ਹੈ।","roman":"Traas sabai taji kai laji kai ari ke dal ke samuhe su gayo hai |","meaning_en":"casting off all fear and mindful of honour, he went out to face the enemy army,","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਨਵ ਮੇਘ ਬਿਡਾਰਨ ਕੋ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਮਨੋ ਬੀਰ ਸਮੀਰ ਭਯੋ ਹੈ। ੧੩੧੦।","roman":"Daanav megh bidaaran ko ran mai mano beer sameer bhayo hai | 1310 |","meaning_en":"as if the hero had become the wind to scatter the demon clouds in the battle.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1311],"number_text":"੧੩੧੧।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤ੍ਰ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਭਯੋ ਨਭ ਮੈ ਤਿਹ ਜਾਇ ਕੈ ਬੈਨ ਉਚਾਰੇ।","roman":"Antr dhyaan kuroop bhayo nabh mai tih jaai kai bain uchaare |","meaning_en":"Kuroop vanished, went into the sky, and spoke these words:","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈ ਹੋ ਕਹਾ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਭਜਿ ਕੈ ਗਜ ਬਾਜ ਅਨੇਕ ਅਕਾਸ ਤੇ ਡਾਰੇ।","roman":"Jai ho kahaa ham te bhaji kai gaj baaj anek akaas te daare |","meaning_en":"\"Where will you go, fleeing from me?\" and he hurled many elephants and horses from the sky,","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਖ ਪਖਾਨ ਸਿਲਾ ਰਥ ਸਿੰਘ ਧਰਾਧਰ ਰੀਛ ਮਹਾ ਅਹਿ ਕਾਰੇ।","roman":"Rookh pakhaan silaa rath singh dharaadhar reechh mahaa ahi kaare |","meaning_en":"trees, stones, rocks, chariots, lions, mountains, bears and great black serpents;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਪਰੇ ਰਨ ਭੂਮਿ ਮੈ ਜੋਰ ਸੋ ਭੂਪ ਬਚਿਓ ਸਿਗਰੇ ਦਬਿ ਮਾਰੇ। ੧੩੧੧।","roman":"Aani pare ran bhoomi mai jor so bhoop bachio sigre dabi maare | 1311 |","meaning_en":"they fell with force on the battlefield; the king survived, but all the rest were crushed to death.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1312],"number_text":"੧੩੧੨।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇਤਕ ਡਾਰਿ ਦਏ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਪੈ ਗਿਰਿ ਤੇਤਕ ਬਾਨਨ ਸਾਥ ਨਿਵਾਰੇ।","roman":"Jetak daari dae nrip pai giri tetak baanan saath nivaare |","meaning_en":"As many mountains as he threw on the king, so many the king warded off with arrows.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਰਜਨੀਚਰ ਠਾਢੇ ਹੁਤੇ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਤਿਹ ਓਰਿ ਪਧਾਰੇ।","roman":"Je rajneechar thaadhe hute saktes balee tih ori padhaare |","meaning_en":"Mighty Shakti Singh went towards the demons who were standing there;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਜਨੀਚਰ: 'night-wanderers', demons."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਨਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਲਏ ਬਲਵਾਨ ਸੁ ਘਾਇਲ ਏਕ ਕਰੇ ਇਕ ਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Paani kripaan lae balvaan su ghaail ek kare ik maare |","meaning_en":"sword in hand, the strong one wounded one and killed another.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੈਤ ਚਮੂੰ ਨ ਬਸਾਤ ਕਛੂ ਅਪਨੇ ਛਲ ਛਿਦ੍ਰਨਿ ਕੈ ਸਬ ਹਾਰੇ। ੧੩੧੨।","roman":"Dait chamoon na basaat kachhoo apne chhal chhidrani kai sab haare | 1312 |","meaning_en":"The demon army could do nothing; for all their tricks and wiles, they were all defeated.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1313],"number_text":"੧੩੧੩।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਨੇ ਬਹੁਰੋ ਧਨੁ ਬਾਨ ਲਯੋ ਰਿਸ ਸਾਥ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਕੇ ਬੀਰ ਹਨੇ।","roman":"Nrip ne bahuro dhanu baan layo ris saath kuroop ke beer hane |","meaning_en":"Again the king took bow and arrows and in fury slew Kuroop's warriors;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇਊ ਜੀਵਤ ਥੇ ਕਰਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਅਰਰਾਇ ਪਰੇ ਬਰਬੀਰ ਘਨੇ।","roman":"Jeoo jeevat the kari aayudh lai arraai pare barbeer ghane |","meaning_en":"those still alive took up weapons, and many great warriors fell upon him roaring.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇਊ ਆਨਿ ਲਰੇ ਬਿਨੁ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਕਰੇ ਰੁਪਿ ਠਾਢੇ ਲਰੇ ਕੋਊ ਸ੍ਰਉਨ ਸਨੇ।","roman":"Jeoo aani lare binu praan kare rupi thaadhe lare ko'oo sraun sane |","meaning_en":"Those who came and fought he made lifeless; some fought on, standing firm, soaked in blood;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨਿ ਯੌ ਉਪਮਾ ਉਪਜੀ ਰਿਤੁਰਾਜ ਸਮੈ ਦ੍ਰਮ ਕਿੰਸਕ ਲਾਲ ਬਨੇ। ੧੩੧੩।","roman":"Mani yau upmaa upjee rituraaj samai dram kinsak laal bane | 1313 |","meaning_en":"this simile came to mind: in spring the kinsuk trees have turned red.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Kinsuk (palash): a tree with flame-red flowers. ਰਿਤੁਰਾਜ: 'king of seasons', spring."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1314],"number_text":"੧੩੧੪।","page":545,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਤਿਹ ਸਮਰ ਮੈ ਬਹੁਰੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ।","roman":"Sakti singh tih samar mai bahure sasatr sanbhaari |","meaning_en":"Shakti Singh in that battle again took up his weapons;","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸੁਰ ਸੈਨ ਮੈ ਭਟ ਪ੍ਰਬਲ ਤੇ ਬਹੁ ਦਏ ਸੰਘਾਰ। ੧੩੧੪।","roman":"Asur sain mai bhat prabal te bahu dae sanghaar | 1314 |","meaning_en":"of the strong warriors in the demon army he destroyed a great many.","page":545,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1315],"number_text":"੧੩੧੫।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਤਾਨਨ ਨਾਮ ਕਰੂਪ ਕੋ ਬਾਧਵ ਕੋਪ ਭਯੋ ਅਸਿ ਪਾਨਿ ਗਹਿਓ।","roman":"Bikrataanan naam karoop ko baadhav kop bhayo asi paani gahio |","meaning_en":"Kuroop's brother, named Bikratanan, grew angry and seized a sword in his hand.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਅਰਿ ਕੇ ਬਧਬੇ ਕੋ ਚਹਿਓ।","roman":"Kabi syaam kahai ran mai tih ko man mai ari ke badhbe ko chahio |","meaning_en":"Says the poet Shyam, in the battle he resolved in his mind to kill the enemy.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਧਵਾਇ ਕੈ ਸ੍ਯੰਦਨ ਆਯੋ ਤਹਾ ਨ ਟਰਿਓ ਵਹ ਜੁਧ ਹੀ ਕੋ ਉਮਹਿਓ।","roman":"Su dhavaai kai syandan aayo tahaa na tario vah judh hee ko umhio |","meaning_en":"Driving his chariot he came there; he did not turn back, eager only for battle.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਰੇ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਸੰਘਾਰਤ ਕੋ ਤੁਮ ਹੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਕਹਿਓ। ੧੩੧੫।","roman":"Suni re saktes sanbhaari sanghaarat ko tum ho ih bhaati kahio | 1315 |","meaning_en":"\"Listen, Shakti Singh, be on your guard; I am about to destroy you,\" he said thus.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਘਾਰਤ ਕੋ ਤੁਮ ਹੋ: read as 'I am destroying you'; could be 'who are you to destroy (me)?'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1316],"number_text":"੧੩੧੬।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਯਹਿ ਬਚਨਿ ਸੁਨਿ ਲੀਨੀ ਸਕਤਿ ਉਠਾਇ।","roman":"Sakti singh yahi bachni suni leenee sakti uthaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words, Shakti Singh took up a spear;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਕਤਿ: here 'a spear' (shakti weapon)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਪਲਾ ਸੀ ਰਵਿ ਕਿਰਨ ਸੀ ਅਰਿ ਤਕਿ ਦਈ ਚਲਾਇ। ੧੩੧੬।","roman":"Chaplaa see ravi kiran see ari taki daee chalaai | 1316 |","meaning_en":"like lightning, like a ray of the sun, he aimed at the enemy and hurled it.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1317],"number_text":"੧੩੧੭।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਗਿ ਗਈ ਬਿਕ੍ਰਤਾਨਨ ਕੇ ਉਰਿ ਚੀਰ ਕੈ ਤਾ ਤਨ ਪਾਰ ਭਈ।","roman":"Laagi gaee bikrataanan ke uri cheer kai taa tan paar bhaee |","meaning_en":"It struck Bikratanan in the chest, tore through and passed out of his body;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਊਪਰਿ ਕੰਚਨ ਕੀ ਸਬ ਆਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਹੈ ਸਬ ਹੀ ਸੋਊ ਲੋਹ ਮਈ।","roman":"Jih oopri kanchan kee sab aakrit hai sab hee so'oo loh maee |","meaning_en":"its whole form was overlaid with gold, but it was all of iron.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਸਕੈ ਉਰਿ ਰਾਕਸ ਕੇ ਮਧ ਯੌ ਉਪਮਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਕਬਿ ਭਾਖ ਦਈ।","roman":"Laskai uri raakas ke madh yau upmaa tih kee kabi bhaakh daee |","meaning_en":"It gleamed in the middle of the demon's chest; the poet gave this simile for it:","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਰਾਹੁ ਬਿਚਾਰ ਕੈ ਪੂਰਬ ਬੈਰ ਕੋ ਸੂਰਜ ਕੀ ਕਰਿ ਲੀਲ ਲਈ। ੧੩੧੭।","roman":"Mano raahu bichaar kai poorab bair ko sooraj kee kari leel laee | 1317 |","meaning_en":"as if Rahu, remembering an old enmity, had swallowed the sun.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Rahu: the demon said to swallow the sun in an eclipse."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1318],"number_text":"੧੩੧੮।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਤ ਬਰਛੀ ਕੇ ਲਗਤ ਹੀ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਤਜੇ ਬਲਵਾਨ।","roman":"Ut barchhee ke lagat hee praan taje balvaan |","meaning_en":"There, as soon as the spear struck, the mighty one gave up his life;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਦੈਤਨ ਕੋ ਮਨ ਡਰਿਓ ਹਾ ਹਾ ਕੀਓ ਬਖਾਨ। ੧੩੧੮।","roman":"Sab daitan ko man dario haa haa keeo bakhaan | 1318 |","meaning_en":"all the demons were afraid at heart and cried out, \"Alas! Alas!\"","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1319],"number_text":"੧੩੧੯।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਤਾਨਨ ਜਬ ਮਾਰਿਓ ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਰਨਧੀਰਿ।","roman":"Bikrataanan jab maario sakti singh randheeri |","meaning_en":"When Shakti Singh, steadfast in battle, killed Bikratanan,","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਅਵਿਲੋਕ ਕੈ ਸਹਿ ਨ ਸਕਿਓ ਦੁਖੁ ਬੀਰ। ੧੩੧੯।","roman":"So kuroop avilok kai sahi na sakio dukhu beer | 1319 |","meaning_en":"Kuroop saw it, and the warrior could not bear the grief.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1320],"number_text":"੧੩੨੦।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਕ੍ਰਤਾਨਨ ਕੋ ਬਧ ਪੇਖਿ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਸੁ ਕਾਲ ਕੋ ਪ੍ਰੇਰਿਓ ਅਕਾਸ ਤੇ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Bikrataanan ko badh pekhi kuroop su kaal ko prerio akaas te aayo |","meaning_en":"Seeing Bikratanan slain, Kuroop, driven by death, came down from the sky;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਗਹਿ ਲੈ ਕਰ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਜੁਧ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Baan kamaan kripaan gadaa gahi lai kar mai ati judh machaayo |","meaning_en":"taking bow, arrows, sword and mace in his hands, he waged a fierce battle.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਡੁ ਧਨੁ ਤਾਨ ਕੈ ਬਾਨ ਮਹਾ ਅਰਿ ਗ੍ਰੀਵ ਲਗਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sree saktes badu dhanu taan kai baan mahaa ari greev lagaayo |","meaning_en":"Shakti Singh drew his great bow and struck the enemy's neck with a mighty arrow;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੀਸ ਪਰਿਓ ਕਟਿ ਕੈ ਧਰਨੀ ਸੁ ਕਬੰਧ ਲਏ ਅਸਿ ਕੋ ਰਨਿ ਧਾਯੋ। ੧੩੨੦।","roman":"Sees pario kati kai dharnee su kabandh lae asi ko rani dhaayo | 1320 |","meaning_en":"the head was cut off and fell to the ground, and the headless trunk ran on in the battle holding the sword.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1321],"number_text":"੧੩੨੧।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੇ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਗਯੋ ਲੀਏ ਕਰਵਾਰ।","roman":"Sakti singh ke saamuhe gayo lee'e karvaar |","meaning_en":"It went before Shakti Singh with sword in hand;","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਬਾਨ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਨੇ ਹਨਿਯੋ ਗਿਰਿਯੋ ਭੂਮਿ ਮਝਾਰਿ। ੧੩੨੧।","roman":"Ek baan nrip ne haniyo giriyo bhoomi majhaari | 1321 |","meaning_en":"the king struck it with one arrow and it fell upon the ground.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1322],"number_text":"੧੩੨੨।","page":546,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਕੁਰੂਪ ਸੈਨਾ ਸਹਿਤ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਦਯੋ ਸੰਘਾਰ।","roman":"Jab kuroop sainaa sahit bhoopti dayo sanghaar |","meaning_en":"When the king had destroyed Kuroop along with his army,","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਜਾਦਵ ਲਖ ਸਮਰ ਮੈ ਕੀਨੋ ਹਾਹਾਕਾਰ। ੧੩੨੨।","roman":"Tab jaadav lakh samar mai keeno haahaakaar | 1322 |","meaning_en":"the Yadavs, seeing it on the battlefield, raised a cry of dismay.","page":546,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1323],"number_text":"੧੩੨੩।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਤੁ ਲਰਿਯੋ ਅਰਿ ਬੀਰ ਰਨਿ ਕਹਿਓ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੋ ਰਾਮ।","roman":"Bahutu lariyo ari beer rani kahio syaam so raam |","meaning_en":"Balram said to Krishna, \"The enemy warrior has fought hard in the battle;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਉ ਨ ਲਰੈ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨ ਜੂ ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਜਿਹ ਨਾਮ। ੧੩੨੩।","roman":"Kiu na larai kahiyo krisan joo sakti singh jih naam | 1323 |","meaning_en":"why do you not fight him, Krishna, the one whose name is Shakti Singh?\"","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as Balram's question to Krishna; the line is terse; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1324],"number_text":"੧੩੨੪।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਸਬ ਸੋ ਇਮ ਕਹਿਯੋ। ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਧ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਰਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Tab hari joo sab so im kahiyo | sakti singh badh ham te rahiyo |","meaning_en":"Then Krishna said to all, \"The killing of Shakti Singh is beyond me;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਮ ਤੇ ਰਹਿਯੋ: read as 'remains beyond me / has not been done by me'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਨ ਅਤਿ ਹਿਤ ਸੋ ਚੰਡਿ ਮਨਾਈ। ਤਾ ਤੇ ਹਮਰੀ ਸੈਨ ਖਪਾਈ। ੧੩੨੪।","roman":"In ati hit so chandi manaaee | taa te hamree sain khapaaee | 1324 |","meaning_en":"he has propitiated Chandi with great love; that is why he has destroyed our army.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1325],"number_text":"੧੩੨੫।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਚੰਡਿ ਕੀ ਸੇਵ ਕਰਹੁ ਚਿਤੁ ਲਾਇ।","roman":"Taa te tum hoon chandi kee sev karhu chitu laai |","meaning_en":"Therefore you too serve Chandi with your heart fixed on her;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਤਨ ਕੋ ਬਰੁ ਦੇਇਗੀ ਅਰਿ ਤਬ ਲੀਜਹੁ ਘਾਇ। ੧੩੨੫।","roman":"Jeetan ko baru deigee ari tab leejhu ghaai | 1325 |","meaning_en":"she will grant the boon of victory, and then you may kill the enemy.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1326],"number_text":"੧੩੨੬।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗਤ ਜਾ ਕੀ ਜੋਤਿ ਜਗਿ ਜਲਿ ਥਲਿ ਰਹੀ ਸਮਾਇ।","roman":"Jaagat jaa kee joti jagi jali thali rahee samaai |","meaning_en":"She whose light shines in the world, pervading water and land,","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਬਿਸਨੁ ਹਰ ਰੂਪ ਮੈ ਤ੍ਰਿਗੁਨਿ ਰਹੀ ਠਹਰਾਇ। ੧੩੨੬।","roman":"Braham bisnu har roop mai triguni rahee thahraai | 1326 |","meaning_en":"abides as the three qualities in the forms of Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤ੍ਰਿਗੁਨਿ: the three gunas."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1327],"number_text":"੧੩੨੭।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਕੀ ਕਲਾ ਬਰਤੈ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਅਰੁ ਜਾ ਕੀ ਕਲਾ ਸਬ ਰੂਪਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jaa kee kalaa bartai jag mai aru jaa kee kalaa sab roopan mai |","meaning_en":"Whose power works in the world, and whose power is in all forms,","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰੁ ਜਾ ਕੀ ਕਲਾ ਬਿਮਲਾ ਹਰ ਕੇ ਕਮਲਾ ਪਤਿ ਕੇ ਕਮਲਾ ਤਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Aru jaa kee kalaa bimlaa har ke kamlaa pati ke kamlaa tan mai |","meaning_en":"and whose power is Bimla in Shiva and Kamla in the body of Kamla's lord;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Bimla: a name of Parvati; Kamla: Lakshmi; Kamla's lord: Vishnu."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਜਾ ਕੀ ਕਲਾ ਗਿਰਿ ਰੂਖਨ ਮੈ ਸਸਿ ਪੂਖਨ ਮੈ ਮਘਵਾ ਘਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Puni jaa kee kalaa giri rookhan mai sasi pookhan mai maghvaa ghan mai |","meaning_en":"again, whose power is in mountains and trees, in moon and sun, in Indra and the clouds;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੂਖਨ: the sun. ਮਘਵਾ: Indra."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮ ਹੂੰ ਨਹੀ ਜਾਨੀ ਭਵਾਨੀ ਕਲਾ ਜਗ ਮਾਨੀ ਕੋ ਧ੍ਯਾਨੁ ਕਰੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ। ੧੩੨੭।","roman":"Tum hoon nahee jaanee bhavaanee kalaa jag maanee ko dhyaanu karo man mai | 1327 |","meaning_en":"you have not known the power of Bhavani; meditate in your mind on her whom the world honours.\"","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1328],"number_text":"੧੩੨੮।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਬਰੁ ਸਕਤਿ ਸੋ ਮਾਗਿ ਲਯੋ ਬਲਵਾਨਿ।","roman":"Sakti singh baru sakti so maagi layo balvaani |","meaning_en":"Mighty Shakti Singh asked a boon of the Goddess (Shakti);","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ ਤੇ ਰਨ ਜੀਤਤ ਨਹੀ ਹਾਨਿ। ੧੩੨੮।","roman":"Taahee ke prasaadi te ran jeetat nahee haani | 1328 |","meaning_en":"by her grace he wins in battle and suffers no loss.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1329],"number_text":"੧੩੨੯।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਸੂਰਜ ਸਸਿ ਸਚੀਪਤਿ ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਬਿਸਨੁ ਸੁਰ ਕੋਇ।","roman":"Siv sooraj sasi sacheepti braham bisnu sur koi |","meaning_en":"Shiva, the sun, the moon, Indra, Brahma, Vishnu, or any god:","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਚੀਪਤਿ: 'husband of Sachi', Indra."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਇਹ ਸੋ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਲਰੈ ਜੀਤ ਨ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਸੋਇ। ੧੩੨੯।","roman":"Jo ih so ris kai larai jeet na jai hai soi | 1329 |","meaning_en":"whoever fights him in anger will not win.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1330],"number_text":"੧੩੩੦।","page":547,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਉ ਹਰ ਆਇ ਭਿਰੇ ਇਹ ਸੋ ਨਹੀ ਦੇਖਤ ਹੋ ਬਲੁ ਹੈ ਤਿਨ ਮੋ।","roman":"Jau har aai bhire ih so nahee dekhat ho balu hai tin mo |","meaning_en":"\"If Shiva came to fight him, I do not see that he has the strength for it;","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਹੀ ਦੇਖਤ ਹੋ ਬਲੁ ਹੈ ਤਿਨ ਮੋ: read as 'I do not see such strength in him (Shiva)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ ਅਉਰੁ ਖੜਾਨਨ ਬਿਸਨੁ ਘਨੋ ਬਲ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਓ ਜਿਨ ਮੋ।","roman":"Chaturaanan auru kharaanan bisnu ghano bal hai su kahio jin mo |","meaning_en":"Brahma and Kartikeya and Vishnu, who are said to have great strength,","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ: 'four-faced', Brahma; ਖੜਾਨਨ: 'six-faced', Kartikeya."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਭੂਤ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਸਰਾਦਿਕ ਜੇ ਅਸੁਰਾਦਿਕ ਹੈ ਗਨਤੀ ਕਿਨ ਮੋ।","roman":"Puni bhoot pisaach saraadik je asuraadik hai gantee kin mo |","meaning_en":"and then ghosts, goblins, gods and the rest, and demons and the like: what do they count for?\"","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਰਾਦਿਕ: printed so; read as ਸੁਰਾਦਿਕ ('gods and others'); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਬ ਬੀਰਨ ਸੋ ਸੁ ਇਤੋ ਬਲ ਭੂਪ ਧਰੈ ਇਨ ਮੋ। ੧੩੩੦।","roman":"Jadubeer kahiyo sab beeran so su ito bal bhoop dharai in mo | 1330 |","meaning_en":"The Yadav hero said to all the warriors, \"Such is the strength this king holds among them.\"","page":547,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach","meaning_en":"Krishna said:","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1331],"number_text":"੧੩੩੧।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਧੁ ਕਰੋ ਤੁਮ ਜਾਹੁ ਉਤੈ ਇਤ ਹਉ ਹੀ ਭਵਾਨੀ ਕੋ ਜਾਪੁ ਜਪੈ ਹਉ।","roman":"Judhu karo tum jaahu utai it hau hee bhavaanee ko jaapu japai hau |","meaning_en":"\"You go there and fight; here I myself will recite the prayer to Bhavani.\"","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਜਦੁ ਬੀਰ ਅਬੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਹਿਤ ਭਾਵ ਤੇ ਥਾਪ ਥਪੈ ਹਉ।","roman":"Aise kahiyo jadu beer abai ati hee hit bhaav te thaap thapai hau |","meaning_en":"Thus spoke the Yadav hero: \"Now with great love and devotion I will install her worship;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਥਾਪ ਥਪੈ ਹਉ: read as 'I will establish (her worship)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੈ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰਤਛ ਕਹੈ ਬਰ ਮਾਗ ਹਨੋ ਸਕਤੇਸਿ ਇਹੈ ਬਰੁ ਲੈ ਹਉ।","roman":"Hai ke pratachh kahai bar maag hano saktesi ihai baru lai hau |","meaning_en":"when she appears and says, 'Ask a boon,' I will take this boon: that I may slay Shakti Singh;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਚੜ ਕੈ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਰਥ ਪੈ ਅਬ ਹੀ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਕੋ ਬਧ ਕੈ ਹਉ। ੧੩੩੧।","roman":"Tau char kai apune rath pai ab hee ran mai ih ko badh kai hau | 1331 |","meaning_en":"then, mounting my chariot, I will slay him in the battle at once.\"","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1332],"number_text":"੧੩੩੨।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਰ ਪਠੇ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਉਤੈ ਇਤ ਭੂਮਿ ਮੈ ਬੈਠਿ ਸਿਵਾ ਜਪੁ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Beer pathe jadubeer utai it bhoomi mai baithi sivaa japu keeno |","meaning_en":"The Yadav hero sent the warriors there, and here, sitting on the ground, he prayed to Shiva (the Goddess);","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਵਾ: the Goddess (consort of Shiva)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਦਈ ਸੁਧਿ ਛਾਡਿ ਸਬੈ ਤਬ ਤਾਹੀ ਕੇ ਧ੍ਯਾਨ ਬਿਖੈ ਮਨੁ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Aur daee sudhi chhaadi sabai tab taahee ke dhyaan bikhai manu deeno |","meaning_en":"he gave up all other awareness and fixed his mind in meditation on her.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਡਿ ਤਬੈ ਪਰਤਛ ਭਈ ਬਰੁ ਮਾਗਹੋ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਜੋਈ ਚੀਨੋ।","roman":"Chandi tabai partachh bhaee baru maagho man mai joee cheeno |","meaning_en":"Then Chandi appeared before him: \"Ask the boon that you have thought of in your mind.\"","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾ ਅਰਿ ਆਜ ਹਨੋ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਮਾਗਿ ਇਹੈ ਬਰ ਲੀਨੋ। ੧੩੩੨।","roman":"Yaa ari aaj hano ran mai ghan syaam joo maagi ihai bar leeno | 1332 |","meaning_en":"\"May I slay this enemy in battle today\": Krishna asked for and received this boon.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1333],"number_text":"੧੩੩੩।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਬਰੁ ਪਾਇ ਚੜਿਯੋ ਰਥ ਪੈ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਮਨ ਬੀਚ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨਿ ਭਯੋ।","roman":"Yau baru paai chariyo rath pai hari joo man beech prasanni bhayo |","meaning_en":"Having thus gained the boon, Krishna mounted his chariot, pleased at heart;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਪੁ ਕੈ ਜੁ ਭਵਾਨੀ ਤੇ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਰਿ ਮਾਰਨ ਕੋ ਬਰੁ ਮਾਗ ਲਯੋ।","roman":"Japu kai ju bhavaanee te syaam kahai ari maaran ko baru maag layo |","meaning_en":"says Shyam, by his prayer he had obtained from Bhavani the boon to kill the enemy.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਬਰਬੀਰ ਬਲੀ ਹੂ ਕੇ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਤਉ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਗਯੋ।","roman":"Sab aayudh lai barbeer balee hoo ke saamuhe tau jadubeer gayo |","meaning_en":"Taking all his weapons, the Yadav hero then went before the mighty warrior;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਜੀਤ ਕੇ ਅੰਕੁਰ ਜਾਤ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਹੁਤੋ ਯਾ ਬਰ ਤੇ ਉਪਜਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਨਯੋ। ੧੩੩੩।","roman":"Mano jeet ke ankur jaat rahiyo huto yaa bar te upjiyo su nayo | 1333 |","meaning_en":"as if the sprout of victory, which had been withering away, had sprung up anew from this boon.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1334],"number_text":"੧੩੩੪।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਉਤ ਸਮਰ ਮੈ ਬਹੁਤ ਹਨੇ ਬਰ ਸੂਰ।","roman":"Sakti singh ut samar mai bahut hane bar soor |","meaning_en":"Over there in the battle Shakti Singh slew many great warriors;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਹੀ ਤਿਨ ਕੇ ਤਨਨ ਸਿਉ ਭੂਮਿ ਰਹੀ ਭਰਪੂਰਿ। ੧੩੩੪।","roman":"Tab hee tin ke tanan siu bhoomi rahee bharpoori | 1334 |","meaning_en":"at that time the ground was completely covered with their bodies.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1335],"number_text":"੧੩੩੫।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਧੁ ਕਰੇ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਤਿਹ ਠਾ ਹਰਿ ਆਇ ਕੈ ਰੂਪੁ ਦਿਖਾਯੋ।","roman":"Judhu kare saktes balee tih thaa hari aai kai roopu dikhaayo |","meaning_en":"Mighty Shakti Singh was fighting when Krishna came to that place and showed himself:","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਤ ਕਹਾ ਰਹੁ ਰੇ ਥਿਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਅਬ ਹਉ ਤੁਮ ਪੈ ਬਲੁ ਕੈ ਇਤ ਆੲਓ।","roman":"Jaat kahaa rahu re thir hvai ab hau tum pai balu kai it aaio |","meaning_en":"\"Where are you going? Stand firm now; I have come here against you with my might.\"","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆੲਓ: printed so; read as ਆਯੋ ('have come')."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਗਦਾ ਕਰ ਲੈ ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਕੇ ਸੀਸ ਪੈ ਘਾਉ ਲਗਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kop gadaa kar lai ghan syaam su satr ke sees pai ghaau lagaayo |","meaning_en":"In anger Krishna took his mace in hand and struck a blow on the enemy's head;","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਤਜਿਓ ਮਨਿ ਚੰਡਿ ਭਜਿਓ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਤਨੁ ਤਾਹਿ ਕੇ ਲੋਕਿ ਸਿਧਾਰਿਓ। ੧੩੩੫।","roman":"Praan tajio mani chandi bhajio tih ko tanu taahi ke loki sidhaario | 1335 |","meaning_en":"he gave up his life, remembering Chandi in his heart, and went to her realm.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਤਨੁ: literally 'his body'; read as 'he (his self)'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[1336],"number_text":"੧੩੩੬।","page":548,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਜਬ ਹੀ ਤਨ ਚੰਡਿ ਕੇ ਲੋਗ ਪਧਾਰਿਓ।","roman":"Praan chaliyo tih ko tab hee jab hee tan chandi ke log padhaario |","meaning_en":"His life departed at the very moment he went to Chandi's realm.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਨ...ਲੋਗ: printed so; read as 'he went to (her) realm (lok)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਰਜ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਸਨਾਦਿਕ ਜੇ ਸੁਰ ਹੂੰ ਮਿਲਿ ਕੈ ਜਸੁ ਤਾਹਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਓ।","roman":"Sooraj indr sanaadik je sur hoon mili kai jasu taahi uchaario |","meaning_en":"The sun, Indra, Sanak and the other gods together sang his praise:","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sanak: one of Brahma's sage sons."},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੋ ਨ ਆਗੇ ਲਰਿਯੋ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਕੋਊ ਅਪਨੀ ਬੈਸਿ ਮੈ ਨਾਹਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਓ।","roman":"Aiso na aage lariyo ran mai ko'oo apnee baisi mai naahi nihaario |","meaning_en":"\"No one has ever fought like this in battle before; we have not seen it in our lifetime.","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਸਕਤੇਸ ਬਲੀ ਧਨਿ ਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਲਰਿ ਕੈ ਪਰਲੋਕਿ ਸਿਧਾਰਿਓ। ੧੩੩੬।","roman":"Sree saktes balee dhani hai hari so lari kai parloki sidhaario | 1336 |","meaning_en":"Blessed is mighty Shakti Singh, who fought Krishna and departed to the next world.\"","page":548,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":549,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1337],"number_text":"੧੩੩੭।","page":549,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬੈ ਚੰਡਿ ਕੋ ਹਰਿ ਬਰੁ ਪਾਯੋ। ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ ਕੋ ਮਾਰਿ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jabai chandi ko hari baru paayo | sakti singh ko maari giraayo |","meaning_en":"When Krishna obtained the boon from Chandi, he struck down Shakti Singh and killed him.","page":549,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਬਹੁ ਗਏ ਪਰਾਈ। ਰਵਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਤਮ ਨ ਰਹਾਈ। ੧੩੩੭।","roman":"Aur satr bahu gae paraaee | ravi nihaari jyo tam na rahaaee | 1337 |","meaning_en":"Many other enemies fled away, as darkness does not remain when it sees the sun.","page":549,"meaning_status":"draft"}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨਾਵਤਾਰੇ ਜੁਧ ਪ੍ਰਬੰਧੇ ਦੁਆਦਸ ਭੂਪ ਸਕਤਿ ਸਿੰਘ","roman":"Iti sree bachitr naatak granthe krisnaavtaare judh prabandhe duaadas bhoop sakti singh","meaning_en":"Here ends, in the war-episode of the Krishna Avatar in the Bachittar Natak granth, the chapter of the slaying of the twelve kings","page":549,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਧਾ ਬਧਹਿ ਧਯਾਇ ਸਮਾਪਤੰ।","roman":"Sudhaa badhhi dhayaai samaaptan |","meaning_en":"including Shakti Singh.","page":549,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਧਾ: read as 'together with, including'."}],"page":549}});
